p.src:
Consider the first-order equation $\frac{\partial\psi}{\partial x}
+
\frac{\partial\psi}{\partial t}
=0.$ Substitution of the plane wave gives $ik\psi-i\omega\psi=0,$ and hence $\omega=k.$ The wave therefore moves to the right. It is useful to label the field accordingly: $\frac{\partial\psi_R}{\partial t}
=
-\frac{\partial\psi_R}{\partial x}.$

