p.src:
Left-right balance requires a second, independent field with its own creation and annihilation operators. Let it satisfy $\frac{\partial\psi_L}{\partial t}
=
+\frac{\partial\psi_L}{\partial x}.$ For the same plane-wave form, $-i\omega\psi_L=ik\psi_L,$ so $\omega=-k.$ This second line is the mirror image of $\omega=k$. Its positive-energy branch describes left-moving particles, and its negative-energy branch must also be filled.

