p.src:
Restoring the differential operators gives the massive equation $i\frac{\partial\Psi}{\partial t}
=
-i\alpha\frac{\partial\Psi}{\partial x}
+m\beta\Psi.$ The matrix $\beta$ interchanges the two components: $\beta
\begin{pmatrix}
\psi_R\\
\psi_L
\end{pmatrix}
=
\begin{pmatrix}
\psi_L\\
\psi_R
\end{pmatrix}.$ Consequently, $\begin{aligned}i\dot{\psi}_R
&=-i\frac{\partial\psi_R}{\partial x}+m\psi_L,\\
i\dot{\psi}_L
&=+i\frac{\partial\psi_L}{\partial x}+m\psi_R.\end{aligned}$

