Let $\phi(x,t)$ be a scalar field with its own equation of motion. In the Dirac equation, replace the constant $m$ in the mass term by $g\phi(x,t)$: (The displayed interaction term is obtained by making this substitution in the previously established mass term $m\beta\Psi$.)  $i\frac{\partial\Psi}{\partial t}
=
